    &lt;br /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;URL:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.maptiler.com/"&gt;https://www.maptiler.com/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freelance / B2B contract&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote in Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;MapTiler is moving toward becoming an AI-accelerated company, and design is a part of that change. We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Design&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the craft and the design practice across our products and customer experience, and help to define the new setup and processes for how designers should work. This is a completely new role at MapTiler!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design team of 5 and make the people decisions that come with it: hiring, performance, wellbeing, career progression and education of designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product managers, developers and marketing, and represent design in discussions with the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurably increase the user-centric mindset and UX maturity of the company: define how we measure it, report it to leadership and act on what you find.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design's transition to an AI-accelerated way of working and help to decide how designers use AI in their daily practice, in line with the company's overall direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design craft, quality standards, and the coherence of the experience across all MapTiler products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design roadmap, which runs in parallel to the product and marketing roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make company-wide design decisions, set standards and quality, and speak up when they are not met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we expect from you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years of experience in UX, UI, or product design, including 3+ years in a design leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading a design team, including hiring, performance management, and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong design craft, shown by a portfolio or a case study of projects you led, and the ability to set and defend quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools in design work, and a well-argued view of where they help and where they do not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to align with or lead Developer Experience (DX), ensuring B2B / B2D products work effectively for both human users and AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to explain design decisions with concrete arguments based on qualitative and quantitative user research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to influence and negotiate at the executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding that good design serves a deeper purpose than looking good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong drive for self-improvement, learning, sharing knowledge, and trying new approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in maps or cartography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the GIS or map industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Agile methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive financial compensation (€29 – €45 / hour) based on your experience &amp;amp; annual performance bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Widescreen LCD, a laptop of your choice, and all the resources you need for your work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours to help you easily balance y

&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; USA - Remote
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it's not just something we provide our customers. It's something that inspires our company. People don't come here to join a culture that's built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html"&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We're headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we're changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Director of Partner Operations, you will lead the operational engine that powers our global partner ecosystem. You will be responsible for building and optimizing processes, tools, and programs that support all partner types—resell, referral, delivery, technology, MSP, and cloud marketplaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with Sales Operations, Channel Sales, Alliances, Product, Finance, and Marketing to ensure our partner strategy is supported by scalable infrastructure and clear performance metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;while this is a remote role, we are seeking candidates based in the Pacific or Mountain time zones to support close collaboration with our West Coast channel leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Operations Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and execution of partner operations strategy aligned to business growth goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable processes to support a diverse partner ecosystem, including resellers, referral partners, GSIs, SIs, MSPs, ISVs, and cloud marketplaces (e.g., AWS, Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and reporting frameworks to measure partner performance, pipeline, and influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Operations Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Ops and RevOps to integrate partner data into core sales systems (Salesforce, PRM, BI tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize lead-to-cash processes for indirect routes, including partner deal registration, attribution, and compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Program &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ongoing evolution of Ping’s partner program, tiers, incentives, and benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure operational support for onboarding, certification, and enablement workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track partner participation and compliance with program requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology &amp;amp; Systems Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own or influence tools that support partner lifecycl

&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; USA - Remote
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it's not just something we provide our customers. It's something that inspires our company. People don't come here to join a culture that's built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html"&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We're headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we're changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ping Identity is seeking a strategic, commercially minded, and highly influential Director, Global Alliances – Accenture to own and accelerate our relationship with Accenture worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact global leadership role—not a regional partner-management position. You will serve as Ping’s single accountable alliance leader for Accenture, shaping the global strategy, executive relationship, operating model, and joint go-to-market plan across Accenture’s Identity, Security, Technology, Song, industry, cloud, delivery, and managed-services organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will turn a complex global relationship into a focused, repeatable growth engine—aligning executives, mobilizing Ping’s teams, and helping Accenture make Ping the identity platform of choice in strategic transformation programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on builder role. You will craft the strategy, create the operating model, and drive execution from executive alignment through customer outcomes. You will build top-down and bottoms-up engagement and convert shared priorities into strategic collaboration agreements, joint investment plans, and measurable results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Global alliance strategy and executive leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute a multi-year global Accenture alliance strategy aligned to Ping’s corporate priorities, growth objectives, product strategy, and regional plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish trusted relationships with Accenture’s global and regional executives across Identity, Cybersecurity, Technology, Song, cloud, industry, delivery, and managed services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Ping’s primary global Accenture leadership point and orchestrate executive alignment when priorities, resources, commercial interests, or customer pursuits require senior intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a joint annual business plan with clear priorities, investments, owners, milestones, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a global-to-local operating model that gives AMER, EMEA, and APJ teams a common strategy while allowing appropriate regional and country-level activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive GTM Acceleration, ensuring Ping is front-and-center with Accenture SAL’s and CAL’s across industry

&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote-US
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is where careers accelerate. We move fast, think boldly, and empower you to do the best work of your life. You’ll be surrounded by teammates who care deeply, challenge each other, and celebrate wins. With tools that amplify your impact and a culture that backs your ambition, you won’t just contribute. You’ll make things happen fast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Director, Corporate Tax, the &lt;strong&gt;Director, Corporate Tax &lt;/strong&gt;will oversee the Company’s global tax provision (ASC740), tax accounting policies, tax receivable agreement and U.S. federal tax matters. This role will manage two direct reports. The best candidates will be eager to learn, try new things, and be passionate about working in a team environment that strives to be 1% better every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You'll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the monthly, quarterly, and annual global income tax provision in accordance with ASC 740.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee general tax accounting processes and account reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute internal controls over Corporate Tax processes consistently, without exception, in accordance with SOX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the preparation and review of federal tax returns and associated workpapers, including the U.S. federal R&amp;amp;D tax credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the calculation and maintenance of the Company’s tax receivable agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead domestic tax audits, and respond to tax-related correspondence and notices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research technical tax issues and document the Company’s conclusions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technology improvements and implementations related to direct tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement process improvements and automation to enable operational efficiencies and create a streamlined close process for accurate reporting and compliance. Be willing to try new things, including leveraging internal AI solutions to improve team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster cross-functional agility and organizational resilience&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;within the Corporate Tax team by championing continuous learning initiatives, mentoring team members, and supporting critical departmental priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key strategic advisor to internal and external stakeholders, partnering closely with Finance, Legal, and Sales leadership to navigate complex tax implications, streamline commercial deal structures, and resolve critical customer tax inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate well within the tax team and across the entire ZoomInfo organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek out formal and informal training opportunities to improve your skills and tax knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of tax experience in industry or public accounting; background in income tax compliance and tax accounting required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree in Accounting or related field required; MST and/or active CPA license preferred;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of time management, organizational, and prioritization skills required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cheerful attitude that contributes to a positive work environment for all team members;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient, resourceful, and solutions-oriented;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with ONESOURCE Tax Provision and/or ONESOURCE Income Tax or similar tax software preferred but not required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to learn new software an

&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; San Francisco, CA or Remote, US 
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Descript is at an inflection point. We have 50M+ users, genuine product-market fit, and a real opportunity to move upmarket—converting high-fit self-serve users into consolidated enterprise contracts and going after the accounts that belong in our pipeline. As Head of Enterprise Marketing, you'll own that motion end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role for someone who's done it before: someone who can meticulously understand what's driving inbound interest, identify which accounts to go after and why, and design the campaigns, lifecycle plays, and conversion experiments to bring them in. You'll co-own upmarket pipeline with Sales, partner with Product on the self-serve-to-enterprise conversion motion, and partner with our in-house Growth/Paid team and RevOps to make sure the whole system is instrumented and accountable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The raw materials are here—a passionate user community, a strong product, and a large market. This hire shapes what we do with them upmarket.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU'LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pipeline Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own upmarket pipeline targets with Sales, with shared accountability for sourced and influenced pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute an enterprise demand playbook: ICP definition, target account selection, channel mix, offer strategy, and campaign design and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a vertical prioritization framework: define which industries and enterprise segments to pursue, in what order, and with what message&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design account-based programs with messaging and experiences calibrated to high-fit accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and maintain an annual marketing calendar that aligns campaign activity to business milestones, seasonal growth opportunities, and pipeline targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source and manage contract and agency resources as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Self-Serve to Enterprise Conversion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Sales to identify high-fit self-serve buyers and design conversion experiments that move them toward consolidated contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build lifecycle plays that nurture individual users into team and enterprise buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and iterate on the plays, offers, and sequences that convert product-qualified accounts into pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Measurement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulously track which channels, plays, and offers are driving inbound interest and conversions, and use that intelligence to sharpen programs continuously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-first marketing ops and measurement frameworks that give the team real visibility into what's working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report regularly on pipeline contribution, channel efficiency, and program performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sales &amp;amp; Cross-functional Partnership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner daily with Sales on account priorities, ABM strategy, and pipeline reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief and align with the in-house paid advertising team on enterprise-targeted campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own enterprise lifecycle with RevOps, ensuring accountability is clear and programs are coordinated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy for high-touch deal acceleration programs—things like executive roundtables and leadership-level events—partnering with Field Marketing on execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to enterprise pricing and packaging strategy alongside Product and Sales, with an eye toward what moves deals forward and expands accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
