&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Carrot: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://c212.net/c/link/?t=0&amp;amp;l=en&amp;amp;o=4420559-1&amp;amp;h=3535232987&amp;amp;u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.carrotfertility.com%2F&amp;amp;a=Carrot+Fertility"&gt;Carrot&lt;/a&gt; is the leading global fertility and family care platform, built on intelligent care orchestration: the right clinical guidance, at the right moment, in the context of each member’s life. More than a thousand multinational employers, health plans, and health systems trust Carrot to support millions of members across 195 countries – from pre-pregnancy through menopause and major life moments in between. Carrot's comprehensive clinical program delivers industry-leading cost savings for plan sponsors and award-winning experiences and improved outcomes for millions of people worldwide.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carrot is widely regarded as a defining force in healthcare innovation as a recipient of several top-tier awards, including Fast Company's 'Most Innovative Companies' and CNBC's '100 Barrier Breaking Startups'. The company is regularly cited by leading global outlets — including The Economist, Bloomberg, The Wall Street Journal, NPR, ABC News, and Harvard Business Review — as a leading voice on digital health, the future of work, and family health. Learn more at &lt;a href="http://get-carrot.com"&gt;get-carrot.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Carrot is looking for a Fertility Medical Expert (RN, NP, or PA) to join our Medical Experts team on a contract basis for approximately a 3-month engagement, working a minimum 15 hours per week in a fully remote role. In this role, you will serve as a clinical resource for members navigating fertility and family-building, providing evidence-informed information and guidance that helps people understand their options and make confident, informed choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will meet with members by video to talk through their fertility questions and goals, offering clear, practical information without diagnosing, prescribing, or directing care..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to put your fertility experience to work in a fast-growing digital health environment, with the flexibility of a contract schedule. You will work alongside a diverse team of medical experts across fertility, pregnancy, urology, mental health, and nutrition who share a passion for continuous learning and an evidence-based approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Own &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide members with evidence-informed information and guidance on fertility topics, such as fertility evaluation and testing, treatment options, and family-building pathways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct one-on-one virtual sessions (video) that educate and present options without diagnosing, prescribing, or directing care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on reproductive and fertility regulatory trends and clinical practice guidelines in the US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in quality assurance initiatives and audits to help ensure a safe, compliant member experience that meets the highest standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the broader Medical Experts team and cross-functional partners to deliver a consistent, high-quality member experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a reliable, flexible schedule within ~15 hours per week range to meet member demand throughout the engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
